      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The article is devoted to an investigation of intravenous analgesia with different narcotic analgetic drugs (phentanyl, morphine, dipidolor). A comparative assessment of the influence upon central hemodynamics, lung ventilation, acid-base metabolism and blood gases was performed, as well as the degree of analgesia in using these drugs. A conclusion is made that morphine and phentanyl are preferable for the intravenous postoperative autoanalgesia."},
